WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.055
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:46.297
CHAPTER 42:
WHY ONLY HER?

00:46.380 --> 00:47.465
[confrontational music plays]

00:47.548 --> 00:49.967
[Ha-su] What if
Mr. Ga finds out what you're doing?

00:50.676 --> 00:54.013
Will you still be able to talk to him
like that once he knows the truth?

00:54.764 --> 00:56.265
[Woo-su] Here. Cheer up.

00:58.976 --> 01:00.686
[Ha-su] Wait and see, Yeo Eui-ju.

01:01.353 --> 01:02.563
You're done for.

01:06.817 --> 01:08.068
COUNSELING IN PROGRESS

01:09.653 --> 01:11.197
[music ends]

01:12.156 --> 01:13.741
Tell me. What is it?

01:14.575 --> 01:16.494
I was torn whether to tell you.

01:17.244 --> 01:19.038
But I think you should know who it is.

01:20.748 --> 01:22.458
Someone in our class

01:23.042 --> 01:24.960
is writing a web novel about you.

01:25.961 --> 01:28.047
A BL novel at that.

01:28.964 --> 01:30.674
It's already all over the Internet.

01:32.676 --> 01:34.261
And guess who that is.

01:37.431 --> 01:38.682
It's Yeo Eui-ju.

01:39.517 --> 01:41.519
[tense music plays]

01:44.188 --> 01:45.856
I said it's Yeo Eui-ju.

01:48.275 --> 01:49.777
[sighs]

01:49.860 --> 01:51.153
I know.

01:53.697 --> 01:55.199
You know about it?

01:56.200 --> 01:57.284
But how?

01:58.911 --> 02:01.705
Mr. Ga, are you seriously okay with it?
Aren't you offended?

02:02.498 --> 02:05.584
That girl, Yeo Eui-ju,
is so creepy and scary.

02:06.544 --> 02:08.629
You really need to read
that novel yourself.

02:16.095 --> 02:17.096
Don't tell me.

02:18.138 --> 02:19.390
You already read it too?

02:23.894 --> 02:26.021
And you chose to do nothing about her?

02:27.147 --> 02:28.524
Why, Mr. Ga?

02:29.525 --> 02:31.318
Why do you play favorites with her?

02:33.237 --> 02:34.238
What are you talking about?

02:34.321 --> 02:37.032
Why is it that
the only one you care about is her?

02:39.201 --> 02:41.787
I mean, why bother with a girl like that?

02:41.871 --> 02:43.747
The after-school class and her novel…

02:43.831 --> 02:44.832
Why the special treatment?

02:46.876 --> 02:48.085
Someone like her

02:48.669 --> 02:51.046
doesn't need to be
someone you worry about.

02:52.381 --> 02:54.675
I think you're sorely mistaken.

02:55.509 --> 02:57.303
She's not an exception.

02:58.637 --> 03:00.222
I would've done the same, even for you.

03:00.973 --> 03:03.058
What you're saying is just a cliché.

03:03.809 --> 03:04.810
My point is,

03:04.894 --> 03:08.188
shouldn't you be focusing more on me
than on someone like Yeo Eui-ju?

03:08.981 --> 03:10.441
I'm Eun Ha-su.

03:10.524 --> 03:11.901
I'm the Eun Ha-su!

03:12.401 --> 03:14.612
[breathing shakily]

03:24.747 --> 03:26.749
[sad music playing]

03:35.007 --> 03:36.759
I'll ruin you both.

03:42.681 --> 03:44.975
CHAPTER 43:
WHO IS IMUK?

03:45.059 --> 03:46.060
[phone buzzes]

03:50.397 --> 03:51.649
[phone buzzing]

03:51.732 --> 03:54.568
CHECK THIS OUT
THIS IS ABOUT OUR TEACHERS?

03:54.652 --> 03:56.362
[buzzing continues]

03:56.445 --> 03:58.280
[tense music playing]

03:59.907 --> 04:02.034
[students chattering]

04:07.164 --> 04:08.749
[Ha-su] Girls, check out this novel.

04:08.832 --> 04:10.501
I hear it's about our teachers,

04:10.584 --> 04:12.336
and the writer goes to our school.

04:17.216 --> 04:18.801
[tense music continues]

04:18.884 --> 04:20.427
-Did you see this?
-[clamoring]

04:22.763 --> 04:25.307
I had no idea. What do we do?

04:25.849 --> 04:27.101
WE WERE FRIENDS

04:27.184 --> 04:29.395
-[students shrieking]
-Did you see this? Is it true?

04:29.478 --> 04:31.772
That was so insane.

04:31.855 --> 04:34.316
-Oh, my God.
-This is insane.

04:34.400 --> 04:36.360
-Come on. Now read it.
-[students clamoring]

04:42.533 --> 04:43.951
[music fades]

04:44.034 --> 04:45.285
[grunts]

04:45.369 --> 04:46.495
The letters are way too small.

04:46.578 --> 04:47.579
EPISODE 14

04:47.663 --> 04:49.123
So what did you say this was?

04:49.748 --> 04:50.791
It's a gay romance.

04:50.874 --> 04:52.710
The genre is called BL.

04:52.793 --> 04:55.045
And the main characters are based on
our school's new teachers.

04:55.129 --> 04:58.465
They have romantic feelings
for each other in the novel.

04:58.549 --> 05:00.467
In the story, Mr. Ga and Mr. Jung

05:00.551 --> 05:03.303
-are in a love triangle over Mr. Yoon.
-[exclaims]

05:03.387 --> 05:06.223
Stop, stop. Please, this is enough. Stop.

05:06.306 --> 05:08.684
[sighs] I can't believe what I just heard.

05:08.767 --> 05:09.768
Oh, I feel dizzy. Ugh…

05:09.852 --> 05:10.978
This is clearly defamation

05:11.061 --> 05:13.188
and a violation of our teacher's rights.

05:14.189 --> 05:17.735
If it's shared online where everyone can
see it, reporters will wirite about it.

05:17.818 --> 05:18.861
[mischievous music playing]

05:18.944 --> 05:20.237
But, of course…

05:20.320 --> 05:21.697
That can't happen.

05:21.780 --> 05:23.449
I can't stand the thought of my own school

05:23.532 --> 05:26.702
being dragged through that kind of
disgusting and disturbing gossip.

05:26.785 --> 05:27.828
[chuckles]

05:27.911 --> 05:29.788
Yes, of course. You're right.

05:29.872 --> 05:31.707
These matters must be handled
within the school

05:31.790 --> 05:33.292
as quietly as possible.

05:33.375 --> 05:34.960
Oh, my head.

05:35.044 --> 05:37.087
Not a single peaceful day
in this darn school

05:37.171 --> 05:39.673
[sighing loudly]

05:39.757 --> 05:43.510
I'll make sure to take care of this.
Don't worry. You can go back to class.

05:43.594 --> 05:45.804
[mischievous music continues]

05:51.018 --> 05:52.144
[grunts]

05:53.187 --> 05:54.396
[music ends]

06:02.654 --> 06:04.239
Huh? [grunts]

06:15.167 --> 06:16.376
It's you, isn't it?

06:17.294 --> 06:19.296
Is it you?
Did you really write that novel?

06:19.880 --> 06:21.632
With our teachers as its main characters?

06:24.343 --> 06:25.594
Yeah.

06:27.096 --> 06:28.347
This is nuts.

06:30.891 --> 06:32.184
Go-ya, what happened is--

06:32.267 --> 06:34.061
So that's the reason why
you looked so out of it?

06:35.312 --> 06:38.690
You should've told me, at least.
You must've been so lonely on your own.

06:42.069 --> 06:44.071
[tender music playing]

06:45.531 --> 06:47.866
Did you think I wouldn't understand you
if you told me?

06:48.951 --> 06:50.494
No, Go-ya.

06:50.577 --> 06:52.204
Tha'ts not it.

06:52.287 --> 06:54.414
It's not that I couldn't trust you.

06:54.498 --> 06:55.499
I just…

06:56.542 --> 06:57.543
[sighs]

06:58.794 --> 07:00.462
I think I was embarrassed.

07:03.882 --> 07:05.551
I was ashamed of myself.

07:08.095 --> 07:10.514
I saw your novel got so many views.

07:11.098 --> 07:13.767
You promised you'd tell me first
if your piece became a hit.

07:16.436 --> 07:17.604
I'm sorry.

07:20.816 --> 07:22.317
How did you get caught?

07:23.026 --> 07:24.903
How did Eun Ha-su find out about it?

07:26.488 --> 07:29.366
[sighs] I really have no idea.

07:30.033 --> 07:31.994
All I know is that she caught on

07:32.077 --> 07:33.412
a few days ago.

07:35.831 --> 07:38.709
You silly girl.
Writing about our teachers?

07:39.293 --> 07:40.961
You're seriously insane.

07:41.044 --> 07:42.838
It's all right. I forgive you

07:43.630 --> 07:44.715
Let's go.

07:45.299 --> 07:46.300
Come on.

07:48.802 --> 07:49.803
[music ends]

07:49.887 --> 07:51.388
"If you don't wanna solve problems,

07:51.471 --> 07:52.806
you can do something else with me."

07:52.890 --> 07:54.433
-[laughs]
-Oh, please!

07:56.185 --> 07:59.271
-What now?
-Geez.

08:03.692 --> 08:04.985
-Hey.
-Eun Ha-su.

08:05.068 --> 08:07.196
[Dan-ji] How can you be so sure
that Eui-ju is Imuk?

08:07.279 --> 08:08.447
Huh? Where's the evidence?

08:08.530 --> 08:11.325
Mr. Ga is quoted in the novel
word-for-word.

08:13.035 --> 08:14.244
You can tell for yourselves.

08:14.328 --> 08:17.039
What he said during
the first day of school is in there too.

08:18.207 --> 08:20.792
Look, to be honest,
it's not much of a crime. Okay?

08:20.876 --> 08:22.044
What's wrong with that?

08:23.128 --> 08:24.338
Don't you think

08:24.963 --> 08:26.548
people like her are weird?

08:26.632 --> 08:28.258
Ugh. So creepy.

08:28.342 --> 08:30.928
[scoffs] Hey, to each their own.

08:31.428 --> 08:33.680
Whatever others like
is none of your business.

08:33.764 --> 08:37.684
Even so, she shouldn't have written
such a story about our teachers.

08:37.768 --> 08:41.271
Imagine someone pairing us up and writing
a messed-up story behind our backs.

08:41.355 --> 08:45.025
Maybe she's already writing a lesbian
story about our school or something.

08:45.108 --> 08:46.610
-[sighs]
-That's freaking creepy

08:46.693 --> 08:49.112
People like that,
use freedom of expression

08:49.196 --> 08:51.281
as an excuse and end up as criminals.

08:51.365 --> 08:52.366
Hey…

08:55.994 --> 08:57.829
-[stammers]
-We can ask her directly.

08:59.831 --> 09:02.584
-Hi, Eui-ju.
-Hi, Eui-ju. Good morning

09:03.835 --> 09:05.087
Good morning.

09:08.757 --> 09:12.594
If this goes to a disciplinary committee,
her parents will be told about it

09:12.678 --> 09:15.305
My parents reading my BL novel?

09:15.389 --> 09:17.266
I'd be gone before they do.

09:17.349 --> 09:18.934
-That's true.
-[student 1] So true.

09:19.017 --> 09:20.894
Actually, I'd wanna just vanish
into thin air.

09:20.978 --> 09:23.313
-[student 2] Agreed.
-[student 3] It sure is messed up.

09:23.397 --> 09:24.940
Damn it, you crazy bitch!

09:25.023 --> 09:26.024
[screams]

09:26.108 --> 09:28.735
[students clamoring, screaming]

09:35.158 --> 09:37.369
This is enough!

09:38.036 --> 09:39.204
What's going on?

09:39.288 --> 09:40.289
[clamoring stops]

09:43.917 --> 09:44.918
[student grunts]

10:08.191 --> 10:09.192
[Woo-su] Yeo Eui-ju,

10:10.193 --> 10:11.445
follow me.

10:20.454 --> 10:21.997
[clamoring resumes]

10:22.080 --> 10:23.999
What the hell is wrong with you?

10:24.082 --> 10:25.584
Hang on. Hey stop.

10:25.667 --> 10:26.877
What's wrong with you?

10:27.461 --> 10:32.132
CHAPTER 44: YOU MUST TAKE
RESPONSIBILITY FOR YOUR ACTIONS

10:49.066 --> 10:50.067
Mr. Ga.

10:52.194 --> 10:54.404
Just act like you didn't know. Okay?

10:57.199 --> 10:59.951
I don't want you getting in trouble at all
because of me.

11:03.538 --> 11:06.249
Since when does a cornered rat
worry about the cat?

11:06.958 --> 11:09.795
It's only right
that I take responsibility for this.

11:11.046 --> 11:12.589
Just say that…

11:12.672 --> 11:13.673
that…

11:14.508 --> 11:15.717
that you didn't know.

11:17.302 --> 11:18.553
Please, sir.

11:18.637 --> 11:20.097
Act as if you didn't know.

11:20.180 --> 11:23.183
Just like the other teachers,
you didn't know anything from the start.

11:24.017 --> 11:26.770
I did all of this on my own.

11:27.938 --> 11:28.939
And, of course,

11:30.065 --> 11:33.151
you have nothing to do with it.

11:38.532 --> 11:40.700
It'll go to a disciplinary committee.

11:41.618 --> 11:44.996
Which in fact is inevitable but be
prepared as to what you're going to say.

11:45.956 --> 11:47.040
And how you say it.

11:50.252 --> 11:51.420
Yes, sir.

11:53.422 --> 11:54.881
I'm responsible as well.

11:56.216 --> 11:58.635
I'm partly responsible for this.
That's for sure.

11:59.928 --> 12:02.848
But you must take responsibility for
your own actions. You can't avoid that.

12:05.976 --> 12:08.019
Yes. I know.

12:09.563 --> 12:10.772
I know you're scared.

12:11.731 --> 12:13.900
You must have regrets
and feel embarrassed.

12:13.984 --> 12:15.777
As if your world is falling apart.

12:16.903 --> 12:19.656
But this whole thing
is not going to end your life.

12:20.407 --> 12:22.534
You may be feeling like it will.

12:23.368 --> 12:24.703
But it won't.

12:25.996 --> 12:27.914
[gentle music plays]

12:27.998 --> 12:29.207
[sighs]

12:30.000 --> 12:31.835
I don't know how this will all turn out.

12:32.544 --> 12:34.337
But what matters here most is

12:34.421 --> 12:37.382
how you go through this,
how you face it and how you handle it.

12:38.091 --> 12:39.342
That's what matters now.

12:40.552 --> 12:41.970
Do you understand that?

12:44.473 --> 12:45.515
Yes.

12:51.396 --> 12:53.440
The principal wants to see you. Let's go.

12:59.404 --> 13:01.072
[Young-hee] What is this?

13:01.156 --> 13:03.533
Explain what in the world this is.
How could…

13:05.076 --> 13:07.496
You turned your teachers into
fictional characters.

13:07.579 --> 13:09.164
How can a student do this?

13:09.748 --> 13:12.083
This is totally ridiculous.

13:12.584 --> 13:14.377
Ms. Kim, let me…

13:15.378 --> 13:16.588
What does she take us for?

13:16.671 --> 13:19.299
How could a simple student
like her ridicule

13:19.382 --> 13:21.051
and make a fool out of her own teachers?

13:21.134 --> 13:23.803
Is that what you call education?
It's embarrassing!

13:23.887 --> 13:24.930
[breathes heavily]

13:25.013 --> 13:27.516
I mean, what on earth are kids learning?

13:27.599 --> 13:31.186
They're treating their teachers like toys!
[breathing deeply]

13:31.269 --> 13:32.812
[screams] Delete it immediately!

13:32.896 --> 13:34.564
Delete it from the Internet.

13:34.648 --> 13:36.983
Think about our reputation.
If the parents find out…

13:38.235 --> 13:41.446
It's an absolute humiliation
to our school!

13:42.155 --> 13:43.532
I'm really sorry.

13:44.658 --> 13:47.452
Ms. Kim, I have something to tell you,
the truth is--

13:47.536 --> 13:50.038
Save that thought
for the disciplinary committee.

13:50.121 --> 13:51.915
And tell her parents to come over.

13:51.998 --> 13:53.542
Tell the other teachers too.

13:53.625 --> 13:55.794
Even [shudders] the ones from your novel.

13:55.877 --> 13:58.588
Yoon Dong-ju, Jung Gi-jeon
and Noh Da-ju as well.

13:59.256 --> 14:01.049
[tense music playing]

14:03.677 --> 14:04.803
Ma'am.

14:06.680 --> 14:08.098
You'll be expelled.

14:08.181 --> 14:10.559
I will never let this slide!

14:16.481 --> 14:18.108
MALE TEACHERS' LOUNGE

14:26.408 --> 14:27.784
-[sighs]
-Damn.

14:31.830 --> 14:33.081
What is this?

14:33.707 --> 14:34.749
[sighs]

14:35.834 --> 14:38.545
I admire your poor reading comprehension.

14:39.254 --> 14:40.255
What?

14:40.338 --> 14:42.257
All right, listen. So you…

14:44.092 --> 14:45.385
him, and Woo-su,

14:46.052 --> 14:47.721
you guys are all, you know,

14:48.263 --> 14:50.473
involved with each other. Yep.

14:50.557 --> 14:52.309
It's a work of pure delusion,

14:52.392 --> 14:55.395
fueled by some incredibly reckless
and crazy fantasies.

14:55.478 --> 14:57.147
What about him and me?

14:57.230 --> 14:59.649
[curious music playing]

15:00.942 --> 15:03.653
Never mind. Just forget it.

15:03.737 --> 15:04.738
I mean…

15:05.864 --> 15:07.324
[Da-ju] Ugh, that little brat!

15:07.407 --> 15:09.909
There was a crazy look in her eyes.
I told you.

15:09.993 --> 15:11.745
I'm a great judge of character.

15:14.831 --> 15:17.334
Hey, are you still reading that drivel?

15:17.417 --> 15:19.336
It's been minutes now. So tell me.

15:19.419 --> 15:22.881
is it a freedom of expression
or an invasion of privacy?

15:22.964 --> 15:24.924
-Mmm. [sniffs]
-Should we go to court?

15:25.008 --> 15:26.801
Is it worth filing a lawsuit or something?

15:27.427 --> 15:28.720
Should I hire an attorney?

15:28.803 --> 15:31.139
I mean, for what charges?

15:31.222 --> 15:32.599
Defamation.

15:32.682 --> 15:34.559
Calm down. Kids can play pranks like this.

15:34.643 --> 15:35.727
Hey, that's dangerous.

15:35.810 --> 15:37.771
-It's dangerous, you know.
-[music ends]

15:37.854 --> 15:39.648
This isn't something that
can be dismissed lightly.

15:39.731 --> 15:41.775
-Mm-hmm!
-No?

15:41.858 --> 15:44.903
Parts of the novel were written
word-for-word without permission

15:44.986 --> 15:46.905
I mean, our words and our actions.

15:47.530 --> 15:49.366
Since she didn't get our consent,

15:49.449 --> 15:51.618
we may file a civil lawsuit against her

15:51.701 --> 15:53.036
if it has caused us any harm.

15:53.119 --> 15:54.204
Mm.

15:54.913 --> 15:58.667
There's no clear boundary for
how much reality should be in fiction.

15:59.292 --> 16:01.336
But it may become an issue
in terms of ethics.

16:01.419 --> 16:02.879
[Da-ju applauding] Hell, yeah.

16:03.713 --> 16:06.299
That's right.
What's the occasion, Dong-ju?

16:06.383 --> 16:07.884
You're acting like a hard peach.

16:07.967 --> 16:12.138
not a mushy peach for once.
You sound tough as nails, not soft at all.

16:12.639 --> 16:13.723
However,

16:15.225 --> 16:17.477
it won't be much of an issue

16:17.560 --> 16:19.062
if we haven't been harmed.

16:19.896 --> 16:21.481
So, the punishment for Eui-ju

16:22.399 --> 16:24.317
depends on what we all decide.

16:24.401 --> 16:25.402
Mm.

16:26.778 --> 16:28.405
[sighs] Geez.

16:33.201 --> 16:34.452
What did the principal say?

16:35.078 --> 16:36.329
It's a mess, isn't it?

16:36.413 --> 16:38.790
[sighs] There'll be a committee.

16:39.958 --> 16:41.126
You'll have to go too.

16:43.336 --> 16:47.090
According to the Korean education major
and published author, Mr. Yoon Dong-ju,

16:47.173 --> 16:49.050
the punishment for Yeo Eui-ju,

16:49.134 --> 16:51.803
will differ depending on
how we decide to react.

16:51.886 --> 16:52.887
So what will you do?

16:56.266 --> 16:58.143
How should we punish her?

17:00.019 --> 17:01.020
Hey, Woo-su.

17:01.104 --> 17:04.566
Can you use that smart brain of yours
to come up with some cruel punishment.

17:04.649 --> 17:06.568
-Hey.
-What?

17:09.654 --> 17:11.156
It's up to each person.

17:12.741 --> 17:13.867
[Dong-ju sighs]

17:15.034 --> 17:17.162
[sad music plays]

17:23.042 --> 17:24.127
Are you okay?

17:28.506 --> 17:30.008
Don't mind the girls.

17:30.508 --> 17:32.302
They'll forget it all in a week anyway.

17:53.198 --> 17:54.199
[sniffles]

17:56.493 --> 17:58.119
[music ends]

18:01.539 --> 18:02.665
[sighs deeply]

18:03.416 --> 18:05.376
[gasps] Oh, Dad.

18:05.460 --> 18:08.213
Hi, Eui-ju. I didn't expect to see you.

18:09.088 --> 18:10.381
I can carry it.

18:11.216 --> 18:13.635
Why do you look so sad? Are you okay?

18:14.344 --> 18:15.887
No, it's just, you know…

18:16.554 --> 18:17.889
I'm just a little tired.

18:18.890 --> 18:21.726
How about you though?
You've worked overtime a lot lately.

18:21.810 --> 18:22.811
You're right.

18:22.894 --> 18:24.687
Well, I've got budgets to plan

18:25.355 --> 18:27.315
and complaints from residents to handle.

18:27.398 --> 18:28.483
Argh.

18:28.566 --> 18:29.651
[exhales]

18:29.734 --> 18:32.779
Still, all my fatigue goes away

18:32.862 --> 18:35.198
at the sight of my beautiful daughter.

18:35.281 --> 18:37.408
And it flies and it flies away! [laughing]

18:43.206 --> 18:44.582
Is school hard?

18:45.250 --> 18:46.543
Want some ice cream?

18:46.626 --> 18:48.086
No, thanks. I'm good.

18:56.511 --> 18:57.512
Honey.

18:59.347 --> 19:00.723
I've realized,

19:01.349 --> 19:03.268
from my own personal experience,

19:04.269 --> 19:06.312
that life is about

19:06.396 --> 19:10.650
having to carry a lot of worry
and a lot of weight on your shoulders

19:11.818 --> 19:13.987
That's just how it is.

19:15.071 --> 19:16.573
So whatever happens…

19:17.615 --> 19:18.950
don't worry too much.

19:20.869 --> 19:22.537
[tender music plays]

19:22.620 --> 19:24.539
[chuckles, sniffles]

19:25.790 --> 19:28.334
I'm not sure what you're worried about.

19:29.168 --> 19:32.297
But it probably feels like the worst thing
that could happen to you in life.

19:32.881 --> 19:34.591
Well, that's understandable.

19:34.674 --> 19:36.718
-When I was your age…
-[sniffles]

19:36.801 --> 19:40.054
my whole world fell apart every single day

19:41.055 --> 19:43.725
But looking back,
the things that made me cry…

19:44.350 --> 19:47.687
and all the things that made me weep
were really…

19:48.438 --> 19:50.982
Not a big deal at all?

19:51.608 --> 19:53.026
No.

19:53.109 --> 19:55.820
I'd be lying if I said
they weren't a big deal.

19:56.738 --> 19:59.115
If I look back
and think of all the struggles,

19:59.741 --> 20:01.868
uh, every single one of them

20:02.493 --> 20:05.788
kind of stuck to me like armor,
piece-by-piece.

20:06.789 --> 20:09.000
And, thanks to that,
I became a stronger person.

20:10.710 --> 20:11.711
So, Eui-ju,

20:12.754 --> 20:15.423
just don't push yourself too hard,
you know.

20:16.507 --> 20:19.469
Don't try to do too much.
And if it gets tough…

20:20.136 --> 20:22.263
Well, you can always take a break.

20:23.222 --> 20:25.391
I'll be right there cheering for you
on the side.

20:25.892 --> 20:27.143
I'll be waiting.

20:27.226 --> 20:30.688
Ready to bring you a nice cold
glass of water when you need it.

20:31.189 --> 20:32.440
[chuckles, sniffles]

20:35.276 --> 20:36.694
It might be tough right now.

20:37.487 --> 20:38.988
But everything will turn out well.

20:39.906 --> 20:40.907
You'll see.

20:41.658 --> 20:44.035
I guarantee it. Really.

20:48.206 --> 20:49.499
[inhales, sighs]

20:50.792 --> 20:51.918
Well, Dad…

20:53.503 --> 20:54.504
Actually…

20:55.296 --> 20:57.465
I do have something to tell you.

21:02.512 --> 21:03.680
CHAPTER 45:
HELLO, THIS IS IMUK

21:03.763 --> 21:05.348
[Mom] What do you think it is?

21:05.431 --> 21:07.475
[whispers] I don't know.
Let's wait and see.

21:22.240 --> 21:23.825
What? What are you doing?

21:24.450 --> 21:25.702
What is this?

21:25.785 --> 21:27.787
Eui-ju, you're gonna hurt your knees.
Come on.

21:27.870 --> 21:29.205
-Stand up.
-[breathing shakily] Mom, Dad.

21:29.288 --> 21:30.665
I write novels online.

21:33.334 --> 21:34.335
Novels?

21:36.421 --> 21:37.797
I've done it since the…

21:38.923 --> 21:39.924
eighth grade.

21:43.219 --> 21:44.554
No one read my novels.

21:44.637 --> 21:46.014
[sighs]

21:46.097 --> 21:47.473
But I found it fun.

21:50.143 --> 21:51.436
It was fun to

21:51.519 --> 21:56.024
write novels and see the characters
speak and act however I created them.

21:57.108 --> 21:59.944
So then I just kept writing.

22:00.987 --> 22:03.906
I hated waking up in the morning
and going to school.

22:03.990 --> 22:06.909
But I got excited at the thought of
writing novels at night.

22:07.827 --> 22:08.828
I…

22:10.747 --> 22:13.458
I know I'm not particularly good
at anything.

22:14.876 --> 22:16.627
For someone who wasn't good at anything,

22:17.295 --> 22:19.047
I wasn't interested in anything.

22:19.964 --> 22:21.549
But for the first time,

22:23.217 --> 22:24.886
I found something I liked.

22:26.763 --> 22:27.764
And that…

22:29.390 --> 22:30.725
is writing novels.

22:33.227 --> 22:35.688
Writing novels of all things.

22:35.772 --> 22:37.899
[hopeful music plays]

22:37.982 --> 22:39.525
Like someone I know.

22:41.277 --> 22:42.570
-But…
-[sighs]

22:43.071 --> 22:44.280
…what's wrong with that?

22:45.615 --> 22:47.742
The last novel that I wrote

22:47.825 --> 22:50.244
became this really huge hit.

22:50.328 --> 22:52.830
And got so many views and likes.

22:52.914 --> 22:56.375
A famous publisher offered
an immediate launch too.

22:56.959 --> 22:58.377
That's amazing.

22:58.461 --> 23:00.505
I'm so proud of you, Eui-ju.
Great job, sweetheart.

23:00.588 --> 23:02.006
But the thing is…

23:03.966 --> 23:07.345
that it's about my teachers.

23:12.725 --> 23:13.976
I wrote this novel

23:15.436 --> 23:18.940
with my teachers as,
as the main characters.

23:20.316 --> 23:22.401
The school found out about it and…

23:24.779 --> 23:27.156
the principal is holding
a disciplinary committee.

23:27.240 --> 23:28.241
What?

23:29.117 --> 23:30.952
This is the novel.

23:31.702 --> 23:33.955
I'm sorry. Read it after I go inside.

23:36.124 --> 23:37.583
[music continues]

23:37.667 --> 23:39.669
[door opens, closes]

23:42.338 --> 23:45.341
A disciplinary committee
because of writing a novel?

23:46.342 --> 23:48.010
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

24:01.649 --> 24:07.071
WE WERE FRIENDS
HELLO, THIS IS IMUK

24:11.492 --> 24:14.954
[Eui-ju] Hello, guys. This is Imuk.

24:16.122 --> 24:21.586
Today there is something I would like to
share with everyone out there.

24:22.670 --> 24:26.215
It is about a novel I wrote called
We Were Friends.

24:26.299 --> 24:28.759
The story is based on
real people around me.

24:28.843 --> 24:30.636
And I took parts of their everyday lives.

24:31.762 --> 24:34.473
the way they speak,
the way they move, their habits,

24:34.557 --> 24:38.269
and interpreted and adapted them
as I saw fit to create the story.

24:38.352 --> 24:42.356
But as a writer, I should have been able
to create something on my own,

24:42.440 --> 24:44.025
but I failed to do so.

24:44.108 --> 24:45.693
I sincerely apologize.

24:45.776 --> 24:49.655
I've only now realized that my writing
may have caused discomfort

24:50.615 --> 24:53.826
and hurt to others. I am truly sorry

24:57.121 --> 25:00.541
I was really happy
when I was writing this novel.

25:00.625 --> 25:02.960
-It gave me butterflies.
-["Why This Night?" playing]

25:03.044 --> 25:06.964
But that happiness was built
on something borrowed.

25:07.048 --> 25:08.925
No, it was actually something taken.

25:09.008 --> 25:10.259
without permission from someone else.

25:10.343 --> 25:11.177
[sniffles]

25:11.260 --> 25:13.846
WE WERE FRIENDS

25:13.930 --> 25:19.060
I'm deleting the entire novel,
to take responsibility for my actions

25:19.143 --> 25:21.520
If I ever get another chance to write,

25:22.480 --> 25:23.814
I will make sure

25:23.898 --> 25:26.817
I write a story based on my own struggles,

25:26.901 --> 25:29.278
thoughts and my imagination.

25:31.989 --> 25:33.574
Thank you for your support.

25:35.034 --> 25:36.244
And reading my novel.

25:36.327 --> 25:38.996
HELLO, THIS IS IMUK

25:42.500 --> 25:44.001
I thought

25:44.710 --> 25:45.711
that nothing,

25:46.504 --> 25:48.339
that nothing could ever stop me.

25:48.422 --> 25:49.924
Not the hateful comments.

25:50.007 --> 25:51.008
[sniffles]

25:51.092 --> 25:53.928
The indifference or my own flaws.

25:55.221 --> 25:56.722
None of it mattered.

25:57.848 --> 26:01.227
I believed I could keep writing anytime.

26:01.310 --> 26:02.853
No matter what.

26:05.398 --> 26:06.816
But now I can

26:08.526 --> 26:09.527
no longer…

26:09.610 --> 26:11.946
DO YOU WANT TO
DELETE THIS NOVEL?

26:14.907 --> 26:16.742
…be the same as before.

26:16.826 --> 26:23.833
"WE WERE FRIENDS" HAS BEEN
DELETED - RETURN TO MY TITLES

26:23.916 --> 26:27.128
["Why This Night?" continues]

26:27.211 --> 26:29.463
[Young-hee] I've asked you to
gather here today regarding,

26:29.547 --> 26:32.049
Yeo Eui-ju and her novel
about her teachers

26:32.133 --> 26:34.677
[Mom] Your dad and I won't
take your side unconditionally.

26:34.760 --> 26:38.597
I believe Eui-ju must learn a lesson from
this if she intends to keep writing.

26:38.681 --> 26:41.058
-[vice-principal] She must be expelled!
-I told her to keep writing.

26:41.142 --> 26:42.435
It's my responsibility.

26:42.518 --> 26:45.271
Your homeroom teacher won't be coming
to school for the time being.

26:45.354 --> 26:46.814
[Eui-ju] How bad is his condition?

26:46.897 --> 26:48.816
[Dong-ju] He probably didn't tell anyone
in case they worried.

26:48.899 --> 26:51.652
[Eui-ju] Mr. Ga,
why would you do something like that?

26:52.611 --> 26:53.696
[Woo-su] To me, you're…

26:55.948 --> 26:56.949
You are…

27:54.590 --> 27:55.591
[song ends]
